codex
Both claims are supported so far. The DE handler preserves the relevant mode bits, and the RAM path copies the requested length without initializing the PUT buffer. The current MTE code fixes its 32-bit case, but still reaches CI at larger-than-one-byte depths. I also found a related GET-side short-read issue.
